## Live preflight and firewall evidence

Commands:
    ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectionAttempts=1 -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ServerAliveInterval=2 -o ServerAliveCountMax=2 arch-daniel "systemctl --user is-active wifimic-server; ss -lunp | grep 6902"
    ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectionAttempts=1 -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o ServerAliveInterval=2 -o ServerAliveCountMax=2 arch-daniel "systemctl is-active ufw.service; systemctl is-active nftables.service; systemctl is-active iptables.service; sudo -n nft -a list chain ip filter ufw-user-input"

Literal results:
    wifimic-server=active; MainPID=33601; UDP listener=0.0.0.0:6902 owned by wifimic_server PID 33601.
    ufw.service=active
    nftables.service=inactive
    iptables.service=inactive
    ip saddr 192.168.0.200 udp dport 6902 counter packets 3 bytes 114 accept
    udp dport 6902 counter packets 0 bytes 0 drop

The UFW status also contained the exact peer-only scope:
    6902/udp ALLOW IN 192.168.0.200 # wifimic-server peer
    6902/udp DENY IN Anywhere # wifimic-server default drop
No broad `6902/udp ALLOW IN Anywhere` rule was present. The peer counter increased from the
pre-send value `packets 1 bytes 38` to `packets 3 bytes 114` after the real Start/cleanup traffic;
the drop counter remained zero. This is independent host-firewall evidence, not a client-local
send claim.

